                            <comment id="16700346" author="nsamelchev" created="Tue, 27 Nov 2018 12:32:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I have investigated the issue one more time and used the &lt;b&gt;segmentLocalNodeOnSendFail&lt;/b&gt; method when the failing coordinator gets the message about itself. This is correct behavior if the network fails. TC tests are OK.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16703088" author="voropava" created="Thu, 29 Nov 2018 12:14:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks good.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16707049" author="sergey-chugunov" created="Mon, 3 Dec 2018 11:35:10 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=NSAmelchev&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;NSAmelchev&quot;&gt;NSAmelchev&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix looks reasonable to me as well. Could you please improve a bit your test and add a check for EVT_NODE_FAILED to verify that event was received about expected node?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After that I believe we could proceed with merging this fix.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thank you!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
